{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>He did not send His hand.</b> He did not extend His prophecy to them, because they conducted themselves with food and drink, as the commentator proceeds to explain. Another interpretation: even though they beheld the face of the Shechinah, as it is written, ״ויחזו את האלהים,״ they were not harmed, but rather ate and drank." "<b>And they beheld Elohim.</b> Rabbi Tanhuma said: this teaches that they grew haughty, stood on their feet, and let their eyes stray from the Shechinah." "<b>And they ate and drank.</b> In the manner of those who cut a covenant: they came down rejoicing from the mountain and ate the peace-offerings that their young men had slaughtered. And for the honor of Moses this verse was written, that they needed to eat and drink even though they benefited from the radiance of the Shechinah, whereas Moses was there forty days and forty nights without food and drink, as was explained further on." "<b>And they ate.</b> The peace-offerings they ate, and the burnt-offerings they offered, as it is written: ״ויעלו עלת ויזבחו שלמים לה׳ פרים.״"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:14.123310991Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}